To reflect a vector across the line spanned by \(\begin{pmatrix}1\\5\end{pmatrix}\) we can construct the reflection matrix explicitly.

---

### 1. Normalize the direction vector  

\[
\mathbf{u}= \frac{1}{\sqrt{1^2+5^2}}\begin{pmatrix}1\\5\end{pmatrix}
        =\frac1{\sqrt{26}}\begin{pmatrix}1\\5\end{pmatrix}
\]

### 2. Choose a unit normal vector  

A vector orthogonal to \(\mathbf{u}\) is \(\begin{pmatrix}5\\-1\end{pmatrix}\) (since \(1\cdot5+5\cdot(-1)=0\)).  
Normalize it:

\[
\mathbf{n}= \frac1{\sqrt{5^2+(-1)^2}}\begin{pmatrix}5\\-1\end{pmatrix}
        =\frac1{\sqrt{26}}\begin{pmatrix}5\\-1\end{pmatrix}
\]

### 3. Reflection matrix  

For a reflection across the line through the origin orthogonal to \(\mathbf{n}\),

\[
\mathbf{R}= I-2\,\mathbf{n}\mathbf{n}^{\!T}
\]

Compute \(\mathbf{n}\mathbf{n}^{\!T}\):

\[
\mathbf{n}\mathbf{n}^{\!T}
  =\frac1{26}
    \begin{pmatrix}5\\-1\end{pmatrix}
    \begin{pmatrix}5&-1\end{pmatrix}
  =\frac1{26}
    \begin{pmatrix}25&-5\\-5&1\end{pmatrix}
\]

Thus

\[
\mathbf{R}= I-\frac{2}{26}
          \begin{pmatrix}25&-5\\-5&1\end{pmatrix}
        = I-\frac{1}{13}
          \begin{pmatrix}25&-5\\-5&1\end{pmatrix}
        =\frac1{13}
          \begin{pmatrix}-12&5\\5&12\end{pmatrix}.
\]

### 4. Determinant  

\[
\det\mathbf{R}
 =\frac{1}{13^2}\bigl((-12)(12)-5\cdot5\bigr)
 =\frac{1}{169}\bigl(-144-25\bigr)
 =\frac{-169}{169}
 =-1.
\]

